# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
#
# Without this, `docker build` sends node_modules/, .next/ and — critically —
# .env to the Docker daemon on every build. The Dockerfile only COPYs the files
# it names, so they would not land in the image, but they still travel across
# that boundary and can end up in a build cache on a shared runner.

# dependencies and build output
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist

# secrets — never send these to the daemon
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# local databases (they are runtime state, not build inputs)
prisma/*.db
prisma/*.db-journal
prisma/e2e.db
data

# tests and their artefacts
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
playwright/.cache
coverage

# QA harness and tooling
_qa
.github

# version control and editors
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
*.pem
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# docs and assets that are not needed to build the image
docs
README.md